% -e over an existence check planned without indexes.  The check asks by
% scanning the relation for the first tuple agreeing with its bound
% columns, as a negated literal's probe does without an index, so it is
% printed without a key, as a lookup planned without indexes is printed as
% a scan.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
node(a).
node(c).

leaves(X) :- node(X), edge(X, _).

leaves(X)?
